eparated-permanence}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{properties-lemma-invert-s-sections}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{properties-proposition-characterize-ample}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{properties-lemma-ample-tensor-globally-generated}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-affine-O-ample}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{properties-lemma-ample-power-ample}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:160ddd1016a906eea82adb4b7152d94f9deca8c321e9e7b16946c946c5e2db07", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e9a3a2bc467f74f7833a571fa79fcde9c12a3b55cb8f14ced5352bf8aec1e60", "source_text": "Assume <MATH_0001> is <MATH_0002>-ample and <MATH_0003> ample.\nBy assumption <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> are quasi-compact (see\nDefinition <REF_0001> and\nProperties, Definition <REF_0002>).\nHence <MATH_0006> is quasi-compact. By Properties, Lemma\n<REF_0003> the scheme <MATH_0007> is\nseparated and by Lemma <REF_0004>\nthe morphism <MATH_0008> is separated. Hence <MATH_0009> is separated by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0005>.\nPick <MATH_0010>. We can choose <MATH_0011>\nand <MATH_0012> such that <MATH_0013>\nis affine and <MATH_0014>. Since <MATH_0015> restricts to an\nample invertible sheaf on <MATH_0016>\nwe can choose <MATH_0017> and <MATH_0018>\nwith <MATH_0019> with <MATH_0020> affine.\nBy Properties, Lemma <REF_0006> part (2)\nwhose assumptions are satisfied by the above,\nthere exists an integer <MATH_0021> and a section\n<MATH_0022>\nwhich restricts to <MATH_0023> on <MATH_0024>. For any <MATH_0025>\nconsider the section <MATH_0026> of\n<MATH_0027>.\nThen <MATH_0028> is an affine open of <MATH_0029> containing <MATH_0030>.\nPicking <MATH_0031> such that <MATH_0032> divides <MATH_0033> we see\n<MATH_0034>\nis the <MATH_0035>th power of <MATH_0036>\nfor some <MATH_0037> and we can get any <MATH_0038> divisible by <MATH_0039> and big enough.\nSince <MATH_0040> is quasi-compact a finite number of these affine opens\ncover <MATH_0041>. We conclude that for some <MATH_0042> sufficiently divisible and\nlarge enough the invertible sheaf\n<MATH_0043> is ample on <MATH_0044>.\nOn the other hand, we know that <MATH_0045>\n(and hence its pullback to <MATH_0046>) is globally generated for all <MATH_0047>\nby Properties, Proposition <REF_0007>.\nThus <MATH_0048> is ample\n(Properties, Lemma <REF_0008>)\nfor <MATH_0049> and (1) is proved.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nPart (2) follows from Lemma <REF_0009>,\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0010>, and\npart (1).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d902a0fa2c9fcb92a1440843ba753b0faa8d20c2c2b38c522399d51b8abfadc", "unit_id": "tag:0892:proof"}
